subproblem.statement:
For all P, n ∈ ℕ, every U ⊆ ℝ^P, T ∈ 𝒟_n(U) (GeometricCurrentOn U n), sets K, K'' ⊆ ℝ^P and reals Λ, σ₀, θ₁, θ₂, assume:
- K is compact, Λ ≥ 0, σ₀ > 0 and θ₁ < θ₂;
- every y ∈ K has some θ < θ₁ with HasMassDensity T y θ;
- closedBall y (2σ₀) ⊆ K'' for every y ∈ K;
- for all y ∈ ℝ^P and R ∈ ℝ with closedBall y R ⊆ K'', the function ρ ↦ ofReal(e^{Λρ}/ρ^n)·M_{B_ρ(y)}(T) is monotone on (0, R).

Then there is ρ₀ > 0 such that M_{B_ρ(y)}(T) ≤ ofReal(θ₂)·ω_n·ofReal(ρ^n) for all y ∈ K and all ρ with 0 < ρ < ρ₀. Here M_W(T) = T.massOn W ∈ [0, ∞], ω_n = unitBallVolume n, ofReal = ENNReal.ofReal, products are in [0, ∞], and B_ρ(y) is the open ball.
